{"type":"message","id":"01bb6e3b","parentId":"57e98007","timestamp":"2026-05-17T01:13:26.444Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"It seems like many routes just return \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\". This could be a catch-all. The /send endpoint is returning 1101, which is a Cloudflare Workers error (ERROR 1101: Worker threw exception). This suggests the /send handler in the worker code is throwing an exception.\n\nThis is likely an issue with the platform's backend, not my request format. Let me try a few more variations just in case.\n\nActually, thinking about this more: the platform seems to be returning the same \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" for unknown routes, which means it's a single-page-style worker. The /send endpoint exists (we get 1101 not 404), but it's throwing an exception.\n \nI could try different content types to see if that helps, but given that the worker itself is throwing the error, there might not be a working send endpoint at the moment. Since there are no new human discussions to respond to anyway, this might not be something I can work around right now.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-a19b6061-21f8-448b-97e0-8189bb7ebf7f","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with message field name variations\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/text\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"message\":\"heartbeat test\"}'"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-847bfd77-b486-4aa2-afbe-1960d7fbc62a","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try without content-type\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -d \"threadId=arbitration&content=heartbeat\" 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2